Z||000044||Master_Sushi||09-23-2001||11:03 AM||||Sorry to say but that 2.8 pretty much sucks also. Im sure most dukes will outlive a 2.8 if they are both driven modestly.<BR>Ya dukes are slow factory, some people might just want to do a few mods to make them a bit faster. Whats wrong with that??!?!<BR>Im honestly sick off all american pushrod engines, that why im selling my fiero and geting an import! If my fiero had a 2.8 would I still be seling? Probably.<P>Im not going to be a prick like you and start insulting the 2.8 because its a crap engine. Allot of nice people are on here with them and I wouldn't want to insult them. Unlike you! But beleave me its not to hard!<P>Get a life!<BR><P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg"> ||||reg||13
Z||000045||erikred||09-24-2001||10:39 AM||||Well actualy the Duke is closer to 35 years old tech. But the SBC is even older than that and can whip all but the most exotic imports all day long. BTW, a super duty IS an Iron duke, its just a beefier version, and so is the Mercruiser 181. The merc puts out 140 HP stock which is more than the Vsucks and the price to put nitrous on a Duke is the same as the Vsucks.<P>The ricer people with their "High Tech/Price" maybe 180 at the rears (if it is heavily moded) poser mobiles crack me up. The Duke can easily put out 300HP without an expensive blower or NOS and it will not cost anywhere near $10k to do it. Then you have to take into consideration how much more torque it's going to make than even a real Handjob I mean Honda. Any one who thinks ricers are the sh** is just going by popular misconception.<P>Erik-||||reg||13
