Z||000047||Songman||09-24-2001||12:51 PM||||Ahhh. One more reason I don't post here anymore.... Always an idiot or two with more mouth than brains...<P>For you folks that don't like the Dukes, ask any of the people who just returned from the Run For The Hills if me and my Duke held any of them up... I was right there with them, and in some cases ahead of them, through all of the turns and straights. And believe me, the speeds were pretty fast on this run...<P>I admit that I am going to add more cylinders into this particular car, but there is nothing at all wrong with a Duke.<P>What is wrong though is people's attitudes. <P>Now that I have been here to look at the RFTH's pictures I will go away again and not miss this sad place.||||reg||13
Z||000048||FieroMaster88||09-24-2001||01:16 PM||||I dont see what is wrong with the duke either?!?!!? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  Mine would hang with the V6 any day.  On the way to Carlisle last year, we had to GT's and my coupe (back in it's 4 cyl day).  We were goin 100 MPH or more, and the duke was right there with the V6's.  Sure it could not get there as fast..but it got there non the less.  Only reason I changed to the V6 is because it was free and i wanted more preformance options.  <P>Anyway..back on topic....cheap duke mods can include different plugs (rapidfire), wires, coil, intake setups.  There is quite a bit you can do to them.  The duke is a good reliable fun engine.  Forget the A$$HOLES. Make yourself happy.  Because in the end that is what matters, how happy you are with your car.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000049||Black88GT||09-24-2001||04:47 PM||||Who do you people think you are kidding?<P>The Duke is the worst engine to come out of GM since possibly the 307 or the 80s Caddy 2-4-6-8 motor.  <P>And how do you suppose you are keeping up with V6s?  You think spark plug wires and a new dist. cap add 40-50 Hp?  No wonder you all own Dukes.<P>Someone said "The Duke can easily put out 300HP without an expensive blower or NOS and it will not cost anywhere near $10k to do it"<P>Thats the funniest thing I have ever heard!! Check the website that sells SD4 stuff.  I think the bare block and head is around 15,000.  I thought even the racing motor SD4 only made 280 Hp, thats after about 100 times of falling apart and DNF's.<P>Laughable.||||reg||1
