Z||000052||qwikgta||09-24-2001||08:38 PM||||Black88GT  **** *** too.  You think you POS V6 is all that, Dodge neons and most every other V6 motor out there today have more HP/Tqe than your motor.  135+hp is almost as common as 16" rims, remember when only Hiperf cars came with 16" rims, now you can get them on almost anything.  I have owned GT fieros and trust me you V6 is not all that.  Having a stick helps you think you are fast, but stock the V6 is not all that.<P> The idea of the thread was for US duke owners to share some ideas that have worked for us.  I posted adding a header, open exaust and more air into the TBI.  These are common perf mods that most everyone can benefit from.  Do I think you can make 150+ hp on a duke with only a few mods..hell no, but not all of us have a V6 to start with and some of us like the fact that our Pontiac has a Pontiac engine in it. <P> Some day I too plan a swap, after paint, and some more suspension work..Im looking at a 3800 myself.  So why don't you a$$holes who have nothing good to say about a fellow Fiero owner just read the thread, laugh to yourself and then go to the next thread, BE PART OF THE SOLUTION, NOT PART OF THE PROBLEM.  Keep you stupid, smart ass comments to yourself.  <P>Rob<P>[This message has been edited by qwikgta (edited 09-24-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by qwikgta (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
