Z||000061||OcalaFiero||09-25-2001||09:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sootah:<BR><B><P><I>[b]READ</B></I> the fùcking post next time!<P><BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sootah, I wouldn't worry about it....kids. Maybe Shaun should leave the beautiful metropolis of Toledo and take a spin down here (providing he has enough nitrous to make the trip) and get his laughing gas powered car spanked by my wife in our M3. I know it's only got a crappy little inline 6 (compared to that beast you drive), but I think you'd be looking at tailights. Oh, wait a minute, the kids location says he is from Toledo AND Daytona Beach...that's only an hour away, ROADTRIP!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000062||erikred||09-25-2001||10:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Who do you people think you are kidding?<P>The Duke is the worst engine to come out of GM since possibly the 307 or the 80s Caddy 2-4-6-8 motor.  <P>And how do you suppose you are keeping up with V6s?  You think spark plug wires and a new dist. cap add 40-50 Hp?  No wonder you all own Dukes.<P>Someone said "The Duke can easily put out 300HP without an expensive blower or NOS and it will not cost anywhere near $10k to do it"<P>Thats the funniest thing I have ever heard!! Check the website that sells SD4 stuff.  I think the bare block and head is around 15,000.  I thought even the racing motor SD4 only made 280 Hp, thats after about 100 times of falling apart and DNF's.<P>Laughable.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WOW, GM must know some good tricks in order to get the shittiest engine ever to win so many races! Wait maybe they did not really win. They might have pulled one of those landing on the moon type hoaxes.<P>150 HP from a duke is not a problem. It can be achieved for a little more than what it would take a V6 to get there, which is alot cheaper than a swap even to a stock V6.<P>As for the prices of Dukes or SD, it cost about the same to build one as it would to build the V6 to the same spec. I have seen many all alum. highly built SD setups selling for $6k or less. A brand new Alum. SD block is $2500 the Heads are about $800 for Pontiac and cheap if you go with SBC. Where are you getting $15k for a block? There are some SD 16 valve Camel Light spec complete motors for sale that cost $15k. There are as many or more parts available for the Duke than the 60 deg V6. BTW, SD motors can put out over 500hp.<P>I am not saying the Duke is better than the V6. I like both motors and plan to build both, just because the mainstream world is always cracking on both of them.<P>Black88 if you could just pull your head from your a** long enough, you would be able to make arguments based on facts. You must have a complex about your V6 since you always seem to be trolling around in these Duke post. Why don't you try to help some other Fiero owners out instead of making yourself a Jack*ss.<P>Erik-<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000063||Black88GT||09-25-2001||03:02 PM||||I am sorry Erik, with your whole 33 posts and everything I am sure you have helped out hundreds and thousands of Fiero owners.<P>Prove to me that you can buy a complete SD4 for under 6k.  Prove it.  You talk about facts, but where are they?  I need websites, numbers, something, anything?!<P>Use the search topic Einstein and look for a post where a Duke owner built his up to around 120-140 Hp then CRACKED THE BLOCK after 300 miles.  Can't wait to see what happens when you get your 200 hp, which all I see is talk. <P>Your all talk.  Where is your 200 Hp N/A smog legal reliable Duke?  hmm can't seem to find it.  Will I ever find it? Nope, well maybe broken down on the side of the road or in the junkyard where it belongs.<P>||||reg||1
